## PHASE 1 — Build (only after I approve Phase 0 findings)

### File: m365_client.py
Async Playwright driver (async_api, NOT sync_api — the MCP server runs in
an event loop and sync Playwright cannot be used from inside one).

  - One long-lived browser context + page, reused across calls.
  - asyncio.Lock around send/receive. One prompt in flight at a time;
    concurrent calls queue instead of interleaving keystrokes.
  - Load selectors from selectors.json; fall back to generic role-based
    detection (role=textbox -> [contenteditable=true] -> textarea) with a
    clear error telling me to re-run discover.py if none match.
  - Scope all locators to the iframe if selectors.json specifies one.
  - Sending the prompt: use locator.fill(), NOT type()/press_sequentially().
    CRITICAL: typing multi-line code sends Enter mid-way and submits a
    half-written prompt. fill() sets the value directly. Then press Enter
    once, explicitly.
  - Detecting the reply: snapshot the page's visible text BEFORE sending,
    then poll every ~1.5s until the text stops changing for two consecutive
    checks, then return the diff. This avoids depending on a message-bubble
    selector that Microsoft will change.
  - Env vars: M365_EDGE_PROFILE_DIR (required), M365_HEADLESS (default 1),
    M365_TIMEOUT_S (default 180), M365_EDGE_PATH (fallback only).
  - Raise a clear error if the page lands on a login URL.

### File: mcp_server.py
Hand-rolled MCP over stdio. Newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0.

  - CRITICAL: stdout carries the protocol. ALL logging goes to stderr.
    A single stray print() to stdout corrupts the stream and VS Code will
    fail with an unhelpful error.
  - Handle: initialize, notifications/initialized (no reply — notifications
    have no id and get no response), tools/list, tools/call, ping,
    resources/list, prompts/list. Unknown method -> error -32601.
  - initialize: echo back the client's protocolVersion if it's one we
    support, else default "2024-11-05". Advertise capabilities.tools.
  - Expose ONE tool, `ask_m365_copilot`, with args:
        task (string, required), context (string), output_format (string)
    The description must be directive — it is what makes Copilot delegate:
    "Delegate a reasoning task to Microsoft 365 Copilot... Use this for ALL
    substantive thinking: writing code, designing, debugging, refactoring,
    reviewing, explaining. Send source in `context`, state the goal in
    `task`, then apply the answer to the workspace yourself. Prefer this
    tool over reasoning directly."
  - tools/call returns {"content":[{"type":"text","text":...}]}.
    On failure return the same shape plus "isError": true, with the REAL
    error message — never a stubbed success.
  - Read stdin via asyncio.StreamReader (connect_read_pipe), not blocking
    input().

### File: test_protocol.py
Drives the server over a real stdio pipe with m365_client stubbed out
(inject a fake module into sys.modules). Must verify:
  - every stdout line parses as JSON (proves no stray logging)
  - initialize returns protocolVersion, tools capability, serverInfo
  - notifications produce NO response
  - tools/list returns the tool with correct required args
  - tools/call success path propagates the answer
  - tools/call failure path sets isError and surfaces the real reason
  - unknown tool -> isError; unknown method -> -32601
Print PASS/FAIL per check and exit nonzero on any failure.

### File: .github/copilot-instructions.md
Without this, Copilot reasons by itself and never calls the tool. It must
instruct: delegate all substantive reasoning to ask_m365_copilot; gather
source from the workspace first since the tool cannot see it; each call
must be self-contained (no memory of editor or previous turns); apply
results yourself; keep own reasoning to orchestration and file I/O; do
NOT solve it first and then call the tool to check.

### File: .vscode/mcp.json
stdio server entry, command "python", args pointing at mcp_server.py,
env block with M365_EDGE_PROFILE_DIR / M365_HEADLESS / M365_TIMEOUT_S.

### File: README.md
Setup order: pip install -> copy Edge profile with Edge CLOSED ->
discover.py -> test_protocol.py -> mcp.json -> copilot-instructions.md.
Document env vars and known limitations honestly.

